---
title: Arachuvitta Sambar
tags:
  - entres
source:
  name: Divya's Nalabhagam
  url: https://www.divyasnalabhagam.com/2025/03/arachuvitta-sambar.html?m=1
---

= Masala

Oil roast @chana dhal{2%tbsp}, @coriander seeds{2%tbsp}, @fenugreek seeds{1%tsp}, @red chillies{8}, and @grated coconut{4%tbsp} in @ghee{2%tbsp}, then set aside to cool. Once cooled, grind/blend together into a paste.

> Can omit chilies

= Sambar

Rinse @toor dhal{0.5%cup} and add to #pressure cooker{} with @water{4%cups}, cook on high for ~{6%minutes} and allow a natural release.

While cooking, make the masala (above).

Once the pressure cooker is free, saute @mustard seeds{0.5%tsp}, @curry leaves{10}, and @green chilies{2} in @ghee{2%tbsp} until fragrant and the mustard sputters.

> Can omit chilies

Add @asafoetida{0.5%tsp} and fry for ~{10%seconds}.

Add @./cook/bhuna-masala{2%cups} and fry.

Add the masala paste, @pumpkin{1%lbs}(chopped), @turmeric powder{1%tsp}, @salt{} to taste, and additional water to preference (@water{4%cups}).

Cook on high for ~{3%minutes} and allow a natural release.

Once cooked, add @tamarind water{1%cup}, @jaggery{1%tbsp}, and @salt{} to taste, mix well.

> add tamarind water a little at a time, it can be pretty tart. Cooking it a little longer helps to tame the tartness if you overdo it.

Garnish with @cilantro{1%bunch}(chopped) and serve.
